PART 3 — RENDERING A SUBTITLE LINE (verified output)
================================================================================
function renderLine(dict, text){
  return dict.tokenize(text).map(tk => {
    if (tk.kind === 'other') return escapeHtml(tk.t);
    const c = tk.hit?.candidates[0];
    const inner = (c && c.reading)
      ? furiganaInflected(tk.t, c.dictForm, c.reading)
          .map(g => g.r ? `<ruby>${g.t}<rt>${g.r}</rt></ruby>` : g.t).join('')
      : escapeHtml(tk.t);
    // data-i indexes back into the token array so the tap handler needs no re-lookup
    return `<span class="tk ${tk.kind}" data-i="${tk.idx}">${inner}</span>`;
  }).join('');
}

Verified output for 彼女は毎日会社まで歩いて行きます。 :
<ruby>彼女<rt>かのじょ</rt></ruby>は<ruby>毎日<rt>まいにち</rt></ruby><ruby>会社<rt>かいしゃ</rt></ruby>まで<ruby>歩<rt>ある</rt></ruby>いて<ruby>行<rt>い</rt></ruby>きます。

Tap handler: use ONE delegated listener on the subtitle container (not one per
span) and `pointerup`, not `click` — click has ~300 ms delay risk and fires after
scroll momentum on iOS. Check event.target.closest('.tk').


