Render the inflection chain as a breadcrumb the learner can read:
  食べる  →(causative) 食べさせる  →(passive) 食べさせられる
         →(negative) 食べさせられない  →(past) 食べさせられなかった
POS codes to plain English (ship this map, ~40 entries):
  v1 "Ichidan verb", v5k "Godan verb (-ku)", vt "transitive", vi "intransitive",
  adj-i "i-adjective", adj-na "na-adjective", n "noun", vs "noun + suru",
  exp "expression", prt "particle", adv "adverb", ctr "counter", pn "pronoun".

"Save this word" writes: {entryId, word, reading, senses[0], jlpt, surfaceAsSeen,
 sentence, sourceType:'video'|'story'|'list', sourceId, timestampMs, addedAt,
 srs:{box:0, due:Date.now()}}. Storing surfaceAsSeen + sentence is what makes the
 later flashcard review meaningful — the learner sees 食べさせられなかった in the
 sentence they met it in, not a bare 食べる.


